    "bookid": 49,
    "chapterId": 137,
    "fileId": 34406,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Burkitt lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Monotonous lymphoid population of intermediate lymphoid cells with regular nuclei and characteristically coarse chromatin, with multiple basophilic nucleoli. Apoptotic debris is often seen scattered or in tingible-body macrophages (H&amp;E).",
    "source": "Helena Barroca",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/34406.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/thumb_34406.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 60989,
    "bookid": 49,
    "chapterId": 137,
    "fileId": 34407,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Burkitt lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Numerous punctate intracytoplasmic lipid vacuoles are usually identified in the Giemsa-stained smear, which provides more information on cytoplasmic features. This characteristic is not exclusive to this type of lymphoma; punctate vacuoles may also occur in large cell lymphoma or small cell sarcomas in the paediatric age group, such as in rhabdomyosarcoma and Ewing sarcoma, where the vacuoles contain glycogen (Giemsa).",
    "source": "Helena Barroca",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/34407.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/thumb_34407.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 60990,
    "bookid": 49,
    "chapterId": 137,
    "fileId": 34410,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Classic Hodgkin lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Nodular sclerosis subtype of Classic Hodgkin lymphoma. Scattered Reed&ndash;Sternberg cells and eosinophils, in a background of polymorphous small lymphocytes (Giemsa).",
    "source": "Helena Barroca",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/34410.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/thumb_34410.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 60991,
    "bookid": 49,
    "chapterId": 137,
    "fileId": 34413,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Lymphoblastic lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Monotonous population of blastic cells with occasionally convoluted nuclei and relatively fine, even chromatin and few nucleoli (Giemsa).",
    "source": "Helena Barroca",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/34413.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/49/137/thumb_34413.jpg"
  },
  {
